  "concept_thesis": "A machine constructs what space remembers: the transparent frame makes space perceptible, and the water keeps an imperfect image of what was made.",
  "visual_hypothesis": "If the arm, the transparent polyhedron and its reflection share one cold light and one axis, the viewer reads a single installation about memory rather than a machine demo; one faint red joint marks where perception begins.",
  "subject": {
    "description": "a black chrome industrial robotic arm building a transparent glass polyhedron above a still water basin. Acrylic rods, glass tubes and oxidized silver sphere connectors; some edges deliberately missing; one connector glows faint warm red; the arm's tool tip touches the structure.",
    "human_presence": "none",
    "human_treatment": null
  },
